) VALUES (
  'ebenezer-scheme-planned-water-interruption-2026-10-06',
  'Planned water interruption for Mankweng and parts of Polokwane on 7 October',
  'Utilities', '2026-10-06', 'Polokwane Municipality', 'https://www.polokwane.gov.za/public-notice-planned-water-supply-interruption-due-to-pipe-leak-repairs-at-ebenezer-scheme/',
  'Bulk water from the Ebenezer plant was due to be cut for about eight hours from Wednesday 7 October while four pipeline leaks were repaired, hitting Mankweng and parts of the city.',
  'Polokwane Municipality announced on 6 October that it would shut off bulk supply coming from Ebenezer treatment works, so crews could fix four leaking pipes on that scheme. According to Lepelle Northern Water, the work was expected to take roughly eight hours and was scheduled to begin on Wednesday, 7 October.

The municipality said the interruption would significantly affect areas fed by the Ebenezer Scheme. The list covers the city centre, Mankweng and Dalmada, plus the university campus, Segwashe, Mothapo, Sophie Mamabolo, Maribe Thema, the ZCC Church area and neighbouring communities.

Supply from the Olifantspoort Water Treatment Plant was not affected and continues to serve the areas on its own network. The municipality said water would resume as soon as the repairs were finished.

Residents in affected areas were asked to use water sparingly and to prepare for the duration of the cut. The municipality directs water and sanitation queries to its call centre. Review Online also carried the announcement.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.polokwane.gov.za/public-notice-planned-water-supply-interruption-due-to-pipe-leak-repairs-at-ebenezer-scheme/", "https://www.citizen.co.za/review-online/news-headlines/local-news/2026/10/06/planned-water-outage-for-polokwane-mankweng-on-wednesday/"]',
  'agent'
);
